.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH alpm-repo-files-validate 1  "alpm-repo-files-validate " 
.SH "نام (NAME)"
alpm\-repo\-files\-validate \- Validate an alpm\-repo\-files file.
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\fBalpm\-repo\-files validate\fR [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-input\-file\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
Validate an alpm\-repo\-files file.
.PP
If the file can be validated, the program exits with no output and an exit code of zero.
If the file cannot be validated, an error is emitted on stderr and the program exits with
a non\-zero exit code.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-input\-file\fR \fI<INPUT_FILE>\fR
An input file to read from.

If no file is provided, stdin is used instead.
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBALPM_REPO_FILES_VALIDATE_INPUT_FILE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
